#: ui/config/playback.py:99
msgid ""
"<p>The device the player plays on, as its audio engine names it. Changed "
"while the app runs, the sound keeps the format (sample rate, channels) of"
" the device it started with, converted by the system.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:113
msgid ""
"<p>The audio API the native engine plays through. WASAPI: its own, with a"
" low-latency shared stream or exclusive mode. WASAPI (cpal): the usual "
"shared stream (more latency), for a device the other one cannot open. "
"JACK (Linux): through the JACK or PipeWire server.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:118
msgid "Shared"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:119
msgid "Exclusive"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:121
msgid ""
"<p>Shared: with other apps, at the smallest period the driver allows. "
"Exclusive: the device to Mixlyzer alone, the shortest latency; other apps"
" cannot play on it meanwhile. A mode the device cannot open falls back to"
" the usual shared stream.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:126
msgid "The device's"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:130
msgid ""
"<p>The sample rate the device runs at in exclusive mode (the tracks are "
"decoded for it). Applied from the next track loaded; a rate the device "
"does not take falls back to the usual shared stream.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:135
msgctxt "process priority"
msgid "Normal"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:136
msgctxt "process priority"
msgid "Above normal"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:137
msgctxt "process priority"
msgid "High"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:140
msgid ""
"<p>The priority class of the native engine's process. High: its threads "
"run ahead of the analysis and other apps, so it wakes on time when the "
"computer is busy (fewer dropouts at small buffers). Applied at once.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:145
msgid ""
"<p>The priority of the native engine's threads (its own and the ALSA "
"output's; JACK's is the server's). High: real-time, else nice -10; Above "
"normal: nice -5. What the user may not set (without the audio group's "
"limits) is asked of rtkit. Applied at once; what was got is shown under "
"the meter.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:151
msgid ""
"<p>The priority of the native engine's thread. High: real-time (a time "
"constraint, as CoreAudio's own output thread); Above normal: QoS user-"
"interactive; Normal: QoS default. Applied at once.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:156
msgid "The system's choice"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:159
msgid ""
"<p>Whether Windows may power-throttle the native engine's process "
"(EcoQoS: efficiency cores, lower clocks, coarser timers) to save power. "
"Off: it runs at full speed with the 1 ms timer, so it wakes on time. "
"Applied at once.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:164
msgid ""
"<p>Whether Linux may save power on the native engine's threads. Off: a 1 "
"ns timer slack, and uclamp keeping the CPU clock up while they run (Linux"
" 5.3 and later, with the schedutil governor). Applied at once.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:169
msgid ""
"<p>Whether macOS may save power on the native engine (App Nap, timer "
"coalescing). Off: a latency-critical activity keeps both off (the "
"computer may still sleep when idle). Applied at once.</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:178
msgid ""
"<p>The native engine's audio queued ahead of the output device. Smaller "
"answers sooner (play, pause, seek, CUE calls, volume, tempo); too small "
"drops out when the computer is busy. The device's own latency comes after"
" it (shown under the meter).</p>"
msgstr ""

#: ui/config/playback.py:185
msgid ""
"<p>The Python engine's audio queued in the output device ahead of what is"
" heard. Smaller answers sooner (play, pause, seek, CUE calls, volume, "
"tempo); too small drops out when the computer is busy (with the time "
"stretch, below about 80 ms).</p>"
msgstr ""

